# FIXED DEFECT 2421's route for a format function, 2026-11-10, lane
# b30-variadic (panel 243's R1, provisional, author ratification pending).
#
# `printf(format: cstr lent, value: i64)` called with `"n = %d\n"` and
# 4294967338 printed `n = 42` at exit 0: past the `...` nothing held `value`
# to the `int` `%d` reads, and the format crossed as a pointer clang never
# read. The door holds both: `say_count(long long n)` writes `%lld` as a
# literal inside, which `-Wformat` reads against `n` in the header's own code,
# and its prototype holds `n: i64` to `long long`; `say_text` the same for a
# string lent read-only. A door that hands on a format it was given is
# refused (`tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2421-a-door-that-hands-on-its-format-is-refused.hero`).
# `printf` writes to the same stdout the runtime writes to, so the lines
# interleave in order.

extern "fixedbugs-2421-say.h"
    function say_count(n: i64) -> i32
    function say_text(s: cstr lent) -> i32

function main()
    _ = say_count(n: 4294967338)
    _ = say_text(s: "forty-two".cstr())
    print(7)
